ProjectALife.DialogueShards["radio_17"] = {
{"r7_mil_ghost_dustoff_calling","military",120,365,0,23,1,{"Dustoff Operations","Any station on the medevac net, this is Dustoff Operations - radio check, over","Dustoff Operations","Any station, Dustoff Operations, I'm on the ground at a hangar with a radio and no aircraft, over","Dustoff Operations","If anybody sends me a nine line I can't come get you - I want that said plain before anybody spends their battery on me, over","Dustoff Operations","But I've got a flight surgeon's manual and I've got a man who reads it, and we'll talk you through whatever you've got in front of you, over","Dustoff Operations","That's all we've got to offer, words over the radio and a book - it's more than nothing and it ain't much, over","Dustoff Operations","Dustoff Operations monitoring - out"}},
{"r9_joke_d120_church_marquee","caller_joke",120,200,16,22,1,{"Caller - Lawson","Marty, the sign out front of Cedar Grove Methodist still says what it said in July","Marty","What's it say?","Caller - Lawson","ALL ARE WELCOME - COVERED DISH - BRING A FRIEND","Marty","Well","Caller - Lawson","So I went - Sunday before last, sat in the lot with a covered dish on the seat beside me like a fool","Marty","Anybody come?","Caller - Lawson","Two fellows and a woman with a baby, and every last one of us brought green beans","Marty","Four dishes of green beans","Caller - Lawson","Four, we ate them - and we're doing it again Sunday, and the sign stays up, so I reckon the sign was right"}},
{"r9_so_d122_coat_on_inside","sign_on",122,165,6,9,1,{"Marty","Morning, it's {time} and it's twenty-six degrees inside this building, which I know because I put the thermometer on the desk to prove a point to myself","Marty","I've got a coat on in my own store, my hands are shaking on the switch and it's got nothing to do with nerves - it's got to do with twenty-six degrees","Marty","So here's the arithmetic, since I promised I'd always show it to you - one stove, wood for it, and about ninety minutes of talking before the diesel and I have to have a discussion","Dee","Say the part about the kerosene","Marty","If you've got a kerosene heater going in one room all night, crack a window an inch - an inch, I know it's cold - crack it anyway - count your people"}},
{"r9_trade_d126_standing_tree","trade",126,205,9,16,1,{"Caller - Erskine","Marty, I've got forty acres with more dead ash on it than I could burn in ten winters, and I can't cut it - I had the one shoulder done in ninety-one","Marty","So what's the trade?","Caller - Erskine","You bring a saw and drop it, block it and split it, and you keep half - half stays stacked at my barn, I'll feed you dinner while you're here and it'll be a real dinner","Marty","That's a fair trade and I'll say so, folks, standing dead ash is the best firewood in this county and it's dry where it stands","Caller - Erskine","I'll walk out with you and show you which ones - some of it's leaning into the fence and I'd want a man who knows what he's doing on those","Dee","And nobody cuts by themselves out there, two men minimum, and Erskine, you stay out from under it and count heads at the truck when they're done","Caller - Erskine","I'll count, and I'll have a pot on","Marty","The place with the double gate on Tanner Road, daylight, any day this month - bring a saw and a wedge, and a sharp chain, not the one that's been on there since spring"}},
{"r9_sf_d128_stove_and_the_list","sign_off",128,175,21,23,1,{"Marty","That's it for tonight, I'm going to bank that stove and go lay down on the pallet like a bag of feed","Marty","Tomorrow's list, so you can hear it before you sleep - wood in the morning, the Sipes place at noon, and Dee's going, not me - and I owe four people an answer I don't have yet","Marty","Those four, I haven't forgot you, I've got you wrote down - Cordie, Hershel, the fellow on the Ekron road with the well, and the woman who wouldn't give me a name","Dee","And if it drops below twenty tonight, get everybody in the one room - I don't care who snores","Marty","Ninety-nine point six, good night, count 'em all"}},
{"r9_obit_d128_hollis_bookmobile","obituary",128,128,8,12,8,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning, it's the middle of November and there's frost on the inside of Marty's window, and I've been told it's a bad idea for a man my age to ride in the back of a truck to get here - so I rode in the cab","Reverend Hollis","Docia Pelfrey, of West Point, who drove the county bookmobile nineteen years - she kept a list in her head of what every child on her route had already read, and she never once got it wrong","Reverend Hollis","Ferd Halbert, of March Ridge, a barber, who cut the hair of three generations of men in this town and charged the old ones the nineteen sixty-four price until the day the shop closed","Reverend Hollis","Roxie Combs, of the Riverside road, who was nobody's mother and everybody's aunt, and who kept hard candy in a dish for children she was not related to in any way","Reverend Hollis","There's a fourth name I've been asked not to read, and I'm honoring that - the family knows I know - that'll do","Reverend Hollis","We'll have the service in the fellowship hall now instead of the sanctuary - it's a smaller room and it heats - bring a quilt anyhow, and come late if you have to - nobody's counting the door"}},
{"r9_ins_d130_canning_second_season","instruction",130,210,8,20,1,{"Marty","For everybody who canned for the first time in their life this year - you did fine, now here's the second-year part, which is knowing what to throw away","Dee","Lids, a flat lid seals once - once, I know they look fine - rings you can use forever, lids you cannot, and if you're reusing lids you need to treat every one of those jars as a maybe","Dee","What you look for before you eat it, a lid that's bowed up, cloudy liquid where it was clear, a spurt when you open it, any smell that makes you pull your head back","Dee","If you don't know whether a jar was prepared safely, don't eat it. Heating it again isn't a promise that everything's all right","Marty","And if it's a maybe, tell me what you want to hear and I'll tell you the truth instead - throw it out","Dee","Don't taste it to check, don't give the dog a bit to see - there's no seeing, it's not a thing you can taste and there is nothing I can do for you after","Marty","Bury it or burn it, don't put it on the pile where somebody's kid can get at it"}},
{"r9_host_d132_dee_three_days_off","host",132,200,0,23,1,{"Marty","Dee sat down on the floor of the storeroom Tuesday and couldn't get back up, and it wasn't sickness - it was three months of four hours a night","Marty","She's all right - she's asleep, she's been asleep about fourteen hours and I keep going back there to look at her, which she is going to be ill about when she hears this","Marty","So I ran the nights by myself and I want to tell you plain that I was bad at it - a man called about his wife's breathing and I asked him three questions and none of them were the right question","Marty","If that was you, and she's still bad, key up again this morning - don't be polite about it, key up and say, Marty, you didn't help me, and I'll go wake her","Marty","And the rest of you, quit telling her she looks tired - she knows - tell her to go lay down and then go do the thing she was fixing to do"}},
{"r5_host_thanksgiving_stuffing","host",136,139,0,23,5,{"Marty","Thanksgiving is this week, as near as the calendar and I can figure","Dee","We're having a can of chicken, a jar of green beans somebody traded us, and stuffing made out of crackers","Marty","The stuffing is my department, saltines, a bouillon cube, and sage off the plant by the loading dock","Dee","He's been talking about this stuffing for a week like it's a moon landing","Marty","Whatever you've got on Thursday, say one thing out loud you're thankful for - it doesn't have to be big","Dee","Mine is that the percolator finally broke","Marty","That's a cruel thing to be thankful for on the radio, Deanna"}},
{"r3_so_d139_thanksgiving","sign_on",139,139,6,9,8,{"Marty","Good morning, it's Thanksgiving - I checked the calendar three times because it doesn't feel like it, and it's still Thanksgiving","Marty","Reverend Hollis asked me to tell you the church is having dinner at noon - bring what you can, if you can't bring anything, bring yourself, that's from him, I'd have said bring something","Dee","He's joking","Marty","I'm mostly joking - it's {time}, we'll stay on the air through the afternoon, so if you can't get to a table, we'll set one here","Dee","I'll read you the menu at noon, you're going to be jealous, it's squirrel and dumplings"}},
{"r3_sf_d139_and_the_generator","sign_off",139,140,21,23,6,{"Marty","Thanksgiving's about done, forty-some people ate at the church today - Reverend Hollis said grace, and it was short, and I'm told that's a first","Marty","Somebody asked me what I was thankful for, and I said the generator, and I got a look - so I'll say it properly, on the air","Marty","I'm thankful for Dee, I'm thankful for an old man who walks four miles every Sunday - I'm thankful for every one of you who keys up just to say you're still there","Marty","And the generator - count your people - good night"}},
{"r3_wx_d140_bare_feet_in_snow","weather",140,155,5,10,1,{"Marty","Weather this morning is snow, not a lot - a skiff of it on the truck hood and the fence posts, the first we've had","Marty","It'll be gone by noon, but while it's down, it tells you who walked around your place overnight - go read it before it melts","Marty","Reading mine, a fox, two deer, and one set of bare feet that went straight across the lot and never slowed down","Marty","You all know what bare feet in the snow means - check your doors, high of thirty-eight"}},
{"r5_trade_dee_stethoscope_coffee","trade",140,300,9,16,1,{"Caller - Gordon","I heard somebody at this station wants coffee, I've got a two-pound can, sealed - never been opened","Marty","Gordon, you have my full attention","Dee","Not yours - mine, I'm handling this one - what do you want for it, Gordon?","Caller - Gordon","Anything medical, my wife's diabetic, and we need somebody who can look at her feet and teach me what to watch for","Dee","I'll do better than that, I'll come look at her feet, and I'll bring a good stethoscope and show you how to use it, and you keep it","Marty","Dee","Dee","The Muldraugh fire station, nine tomorrow, Gordon","Marty","Dee, that's your stethoscope","Dee","I have a spare","Marty","You do not have a spare","Dee","Well, now I have coffee, we'll make it in a saucepan with a clean sock, since somebody's percolator is dead"}},
{"r9_joke_d140_speed_limit_sign","caller_joke",140,220,16,22,1,{"Caller - Elmo","Marty, there's a thirty-five mile an hour sign on the Muldraugh road and I obey it","Marty","You obey it","Caller - Elmo","Every time, to the number, my wife says I'm out of my mind","Marty","There's no law left on that road, Elmo","Caller - Elmo","That's exactly it, it's the last law there is and it's got my name on it as much as anybody's, and I'd hate to be the one that let it go","Marty","Anybody ever pass you?","Caller - Elmo","A fellow did last week, doing about sixty, and I'll tell you the truth, Marty, I was hot about it for two solid days"}},
{"r9_sil_d140_generator_down_hand_over_mic","silence",140,215,0,23,1,{"Marty","Hold on, I've got to go turn her down, give me two minutes","Dee","Your hand's not over it, Marty","Marty","Well, it is now","Marty","All right, we're back, and we're at about half the volume we were, so turn yours up - I'd rather you had to lean in than have me quit at nine"}},
{"r3_host_d142_hollis_advent","host",142,142,9,12,8,{"Reverend Hollis","Today's the first Sunday of Advent, that's the waiting season, for those who didn't grow up with it - four Sundays of waiting, before Christmas","Reverend Hollis","We used to light a candle every week and we still do - a real one, in a jar, in a back window where the road can't see","Reverend Hollis","People tell me we've done nothing but wait since July - wait on the Army - wait on the power - wait on somebody to come up the road","Reverend Hollis","The difference with Advent is you're not waiting on somebody to come save you - you're getting the house ready - you sweep, you set the table, you don't just sit","Reverend Hollis","So this week, get something ready - a room, a stack of wood - a place at the table for whoever comes next"}},
{"r9_host_d148_battery_and_a_truck","host",148,210,0,23,1,{"Marty","If you lost me for two days, here's what happened and here's who fixed it","Marty","The generator quit Wednesday evening in the middle of a sentence - not out of fuel - quit, and I stood in the dark and said some things about Lloyd's wiring that Lloyd didn't deserve","Marty","Then a man I've never met drove up here from the Ekron road with two car batteries in a milk crate and a thing he built himself in a coffee can","Caller - Estel","It ain't pretty, Marty","Marty","It is not pretty, but the rig runs off the batteries now and we charge the batteries off a truck idling twenty minutes, and twenty minutes of idling is a lot cheaper than four hours of that generator","Marty","Estel Combs, second time on this radio he's fixed something of mine without being asked - he wouldn't take anything for it, so I loaded thirty pound of dog food in his truck while he was talking"}},
{"r5_host_ledger_paid_in_full","host",150,300,0,23,1,{"Marty","I've got the charge-account ledger from the store here on the desk - eighty-one accounts, going back to nineteen seventy-one","Marty","I'm going to read out the names and square them - it'll take a few minutes, bear with me","Marty","Sullivan farm, paid - Arnold Pickett, paid - Gaylene Moore, paid - Gaylene, your eighty-eight check bounced, it's fine","Marty","Reverend Hollis, forty dollars of birdseed, paid in full - Reverend, I know good and well that birdseed was for the church squirrels you swore you weren't feeding","Dee","Some of these names were on the Reverend's Sunday lists","Marty","I know which ones, I'm reading them anyway - Tom Whitt, paid in full - Coralee Banks, paid in full","Marty","Everybody in this book is square with Colburn Feed, every single one - I'm closing it now"}},
{"r5_trade_kids_coat_swap_pam","trade",150,200,9,16,1,{"Caller - Pam","Dee, we're doing a coat swap for kids - bring what they've outgrown and take the next size up","Dee","Pam, that's wonderful - where?","Caller - Pam","The side door of the Riverside elementary gym, eleven in the morning - we've pulled the bleachers out and sorted everything by size on them","Caller - Pam","My boy's grown two sizes since July, nobody told him to stop","Dee","Bring hats and mittens too, if you've got them, little ones lose heat off their heads and hands faster than you'd think","Marty","And if you haven't got anything to swap, go anyway - Pam's not checking","Caller - Pam","I'm not checking"}},
{"r5_host_truck_in_the_lot","host",150,300,0,23,1,{"Marty","I'll be honest with you tonight, I nearly didn't come on","Marty","Nothing happened, nobody got hurt, I just sat in the truck out in the lot for an hour and couldn't make myself walk in","Dee","He came in eventually, he sat in the truck, and I sat in the doorway, and we both pretended we weren't waiting on each other","Marty","I'm not asking for anything, I just figure some of you have sat in a truck like that","Dee","If you're sitting in your own truck tonight, that's allowed - just come in after","Marty","Alright, we're on, let's take some calls"}},
{"r5_obit_caller_royce_ferrets","obituary",150,400,8,21,1,{"Caller - Mona","Marty, last fall you read a note on the air that said, 'Have ferrets - will trade ferrets'","Marty","I did, I've thought about it more than I'd like to admit","Caller - Mona","That was my brother - Royce Mathis, of Riverside, he wrote that note","Caller - Mona","He was a strange man, forty-seven, never married, nine ferrets, and every one of them had a middle name - he fixed my furnace every winter and wouldn't let me thank him","Caller - Mona","He passed in February - pneumonia - not them, he'd want that clear","Caller - Mona","So I'd like him read - Royce Mathis, a strange man and a good one, and I've got the ferrets now, heh - so the offer stands","Dee","Royce Mathis, we'll put the ferrets back on the Trading Post for you, Mona"}},
{"r5_trade_merle_carburetor_sorghum","trade",150,300,9,16,1,{"Caller - Merle","Marty, I've got a generator with a gummed-up carburetor, I've taken it apart twice and made it worse twice","Marty","So what are you looking for, Merle?","Caller - Merle","Somebody who knows small engines, or a carburetor off anything with a five-horse motor - a tiller, a pressure washer, a go-kart","Caller - Merle","I've got a dozen jars of sorghum, made it myself in October, cooked it down in the old pan in the yard","Dee","Merle, don't run that generator in the garage while you test it - door open doesn't count, outside, and away from the windows","Caller - Merle","That's how my cousin's family went, back in January, I heard you, Dee","Marty","The Ekron Baptist church lot, two in the afternoon, sorghum for a carburetor, or for a man who can fix one"}},
{"r9_obit_d150_caller_neighbor_dog","obituary",150,300,8,21,1,{"Caller - Lawson","Marty, I've got a dog that isn't mine and I'd like to read the man he belongs to","Marty","Go ahead","Caller - Lawson","Gilmer Pack, he lived across the road from me thirty-one years and we were not friends - we had a property line argument in eighty-four that we never did settle","Caller - Lawson","In November he come over and knocked and asked would I take the dog if anything happened - that's the longest conversation we'd had since eighty-four, took about a minute and a half","Marty","And you took the dog","Caller - Lawson","His name's Roscoe and he sleeps on my side of the line, which Gilmer would have had something to say about","Caller - Lawson","Gilmer Pack, he asked me and not anybody else, I've thought about that about forty times since and I still can't get to the bottom of it","Marty","Gilmer Pack, of the Halbert Street road, he knew who to ask - Lawson, I'd say that about covers it"}},
{"r3_so_d151_new_hours","sign_on",151,200,6,8,1,{"Marty","Morning, ninety-nine point six - this is Marty","Marty","New hours, starting today, seven to nine in the morning - nine to eleven at night - that's all, the diesel isn't coming like it did, and I'd rather be short than gone","Marty","If you need Dee in between, she's still on nineteen, off and on - mostly on","Marty","It's {time}, the scanner's got nothing, the classifieds have got three things - count your people - let's go"}},
{"r3_host_d151_one_breath","host",151,260,9,21,1,{"Marty","You'll notice I sound like a bullfrog - Dee says it's my voice giving out from five months of talking - I say it's the cold","Dee","It's the talking","Marty","So I'm doing less of it - new rule, if you key up on nineteen and it isn't an emergency, keep it to one breath - your place, your number, what you need, then let go","Marty","That's how the good ones did it on the scanner, back when there were good ones - one breath - try it","Caller - Harold","Harold, Ekron road, eleven, need an elbow for a wood stove pipe","Marty","That's how it's done - Harold, I've got two - come get one"}},
{"r3_ins_d151_frostbite","instruction",151,240,0,23,1,{"Dee","Frostbite, fingers, toes, ears, the nose, first it goes white and waxy and numb - that's when you get inside","Dee","Warm it in warm water, not hot, water you could rest your elbow in and be comfortable - it'll hurt coming back - that's good, hurting means it's alive","Dee","Don't rub it, don't rub snow on it, whoever's granddaddy told you to - and don't warm it by the stove, you can't feel it, and you'll burn it","Dee","Don't thaw it out if there's a chance it'll freeze again before you get home - thawed and refrozen is worse than frozen - get home first"}},
{"r3_wx_d151_nine_days_gray","weather",151,175,6,10,1,{"Marty","Weather - gray, it's been gray nine days running, I've forgotten what color the sky's supposed to be - Dee says blue, I'm taking her word for it","Marty","Thirty-one this morning, maybe forty this afternoon - Drizzle that freezes on the windshield and melts off by noon","Marty","The sun's down before five now, plan your day backward from that - be where you're sleeping by half past four, and I mean inside with the door shut, not walking up to it"}},
{"r3_sil_d151_snow_quiet","silence",151,240,23,4,1,{"99.6 FM","(Dead quiet, snow on the ground outside, and even the static sounds far away)"}},
{"r9_trade_d152_four_notes_three_nothing","trade",152,230,9,16,1,{"Marty","Trading Post, four notes came through the slot this week - four, and I'm going to read all four of them, including the three that aren't trades","Marty","One, a family at Ekron has a pressure canner they'll lend out - lend, not trade, you bring it back and you bring it back clean","Marty","Two, a woman in Rosewood wrote, and this is all it says - nothing to trade, just wanted my name in the pile with everybody else's - it's signed Hettie","Marty","Three says, no trade, is anybody alive on the Valley Station road, and it doesn't have a name on it at all","Marty","Four is a child's handwriting and it says they've got a turtle","Dee","Read the turtle one again","Marty","They've got a turtle, that's it, that's all it says, and I want to say to whoever's got that turtle, hang on to him, he's not for trade","Marty","Hettie in Rosewood, your name's in the pile, it's in the ledger and it's on the air, that's the Trading Post this week - it'll be longer in the spring"}},
{"r5_joke_sonny_santa_shots","caller_joke",155,169,16,21,4,{"Caller - Sonny","Marty, Dee, my daughter's got a question, and I promised her I'd call the radio","Dee","What does she want to know, Sonny?","Caller - Sonny","She wants to know if Santa got bit","Dee","Tell her no, tell her the nurse on the radio gave Santa his shots herself back in November, and he sat real still for it","Caller - Sonny","She says, how does he get past the Army?","Marty","Tell her he's got a pass - always has, they salute him at the gate","Caller - Sonny","She says okay, she says thank you - she says Dee better check the reindeer too","Dee","Tell her I'm on it"}},
{"r9_ins_d155_sleeping_cold_two","instruction",155,235,8,20,1,{"Marty","Sleeping cold, everybody's figured out the one warm room by now - this is the next part, which is how to actually sleep in it instead of laying there","Dee","Hat, in the bed - I know how you feel about it - wear the hat, and something over your ears if the hat won't stay on","Dee","Don't get in cold, heat a rock or a brick by the stove, wrap it in a towel and put it down at the foot twenty minutes before you get in - water jug works too if the lid's good","Dee","Two to a bed and three if you've got them - kids in the middle, and put the person who gets up at night on the outside so nobody gets climbed over","Marty","And something under you, the cold comes up out of the floor and out of a mattress on the floor - cardboard, feed sacks, a folded quilt, under you matters more than over you","Dee","Go in the bed dry, change out of anything you sweated in, even if you have to stand there freezing to do it - wet clothes in a bed will keep you cold all night","Marty","And eat something before you lay down, even a little - a body with nothing in it can't make heat"}},
{"r9_obit_d156_hollis_santa_suit","obituary",156,156,8,12,8,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning, two Sundays before Christmas, and I've been going back and forth all week on whether to say that out loud - I've decided to say it, it's two Sundays before Christmas","Reverend Hollis","Bascom Fields, of no address I can give you, who came into this county in August with nothing and worked for his supper at eleven different houses that I know of, and never once asked anybody for the second plate","Reverend Hollis","Lurline Whitt, of Muldraugh, who played the piano at Little Bethel forty-one years and could not read a note of music - she'd have you hum it once and then she had it","Reverend Hollis","Wilgus Pack, of March Ridge, who put on the suit at the Lions Club Christmas party twenty-two years running - it's in his attic in a garment bag with mothballs in the pockets - his daughter told me that","Reverend Hollis","She asked me what to do with it and I told her I didn't know - I've thought about it all week and I still don't know, and I'd rather tell you that than make something up","Reverend Hollis","If any man in this county wants to wear it this year, she'll give it to you - that's as far as I got"}},
{"r9_joke_d158_zeroed_the_scope","caller_joke",158,240,16,22,1,{"Caller - Erskine","Marty, I lost the barn in November, lost the truck in December, the transmission went out of it up on the ridge","Marty","That's a bad run","Caller - Erskine","And in January somebody took a little four power scope off my deer rifle out of the back of the truck","Marty","Out of everything you just said","Caller - Erskine","It's the scope, I'd finally got it zeroed - twenty-two years I've had that rifle and I got it right in October and then somebody took it in January","Marty","The barn though, Erskine","Caller - Erskine","The barn was insured, not that it matters, but the scope was zeroed"}},
{"r9_mb_d158_choir_in_the_cold","music_bridge",158,225,0,23,1,{"Marty","Instead of music tonight, Reverend Hollis sent word he'd hold the phone up in the fellowship hall while they practice - so this is four people and a stove","Reverend Hollis","There's six of us, two are just here for the stove and they've been honest about it","Marty","Go ahead, then, I'll be quiet","Reverend Hollis","They won't sing with a radio on them, so I'm going to set this down on the pew and you can hear whatever you hear, and that'll have to do","Marty","That's a stove door, that's somebody's chair - that's about as close to music as this station's got","Reverend Hollis","They're singing now - don't say anything, Marty"}},
{"r9_host_d160_name_every_night","host",160,215,0,23,1,{"Dee","I want to say something about the names I read at the end of the night, because a man asked me yesterday why I bother","Dee","I read the same nine names every night, nine people that somebody's looking for, and no, not one of those nine has ever answered me - not once in five months","Dee","My brother Curtis is on that list, he's a mechanic at the motor pool at Fort Knox and the last thing he said to me was that he wanted to borrow my truck to move a couch","Dee","I'm going to keep saying all nine, I'm not going to tell any of you what to expect, because I don't know, and I've quit guessing out loud","Marty","Say them","Dee","Curtis Meade - Bobby Gaddis - Arlene Ison - Dwight Whitt - Sudie Kite, bud Lawson and Martha Lawson - the Tackett boys, both of them - that's tonight's"}},
{"r3_host_d163_hollis_longest_night","host",163,163,9,12,10,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning - Tuesday is the longest night of the year, the shortest day - some churches used to hold a service for it, for the folks who find Christmas hard","Reverend Hollis","I expect that's most of us this year, so Tuesday night we sit up at the fellowship hall until it's light, then go home","Reverend Hollis","Bring a blanket, bring the name of whoever you're missing, if you want to - you can say it out loud or not, there's no program - I've been told I'm not allowed to talk","Marty","Dee told him that","Reverend Hollis","Dee tells me a great many things - Tuesday - longest night, we'll sit up"}},
{"r3_mb_d163_humming_choir","music_bridge",163,169,16,21,6,{"Marty","The children from the church are here, and they asked to do something for the radio - they're not going to sing - Dee's rule, they're going to hum, soft","Dee","It's a noise thing, Marty, nothing to do with me","Marty","It's Dee's rule - go ahead, kids","99.6 FM","(A dozen children humming something slow and familiar, off-key, and one of them giggling in the middle)","Marty","That was the March Ridge fellowship hall children's choir, the giggle was Dustin - he's been talked to"}},
{"r5_host_christmas_twine_tags","host",163,169,0,23,5,{"Marty","It's Christmas week, we don't have a tree, but Dee strung a length of baling twine across the top of the transmitter with feed tags hanging off it","Dee","Each tag has a name on it, people who called this station once and never called back","Marty","There are forty-some tags, we ran out of twine, so the rest are thumbtacked around the doorframe","Dee","If your name's on one and you're still out there, call in - I'll take you down off that doorframe myself and be glad to do it","Marty","Merry Christmas from March Ridge, to whoever's listening - keep your stove going and your chimney swept"}},
{"r3_so_d169_socks_and_sorghum","sign_on",169,169,6,9,10,{"Marty","Merry Christmas, it's {time}, it's nine degrees, and I've been up since four because somebody left something on the loading dock","Marty","It's a pair of wool socks, a jar of sorghum, and a note - the note says, 'For the radio man and the nurse - don't fight over the socks'","Dee","I get the socks","Marty","We're fighting over the socks - Merry Christmas from March Ridge - Reverend Hollis says dinner's at the church today, service is tomorrow, and nobody has to sing"}},
{"r3_sf_d169_bigger_than_the_store","sign_off",169,169,22,23,10,{"Marty","Christmas is about gone - Dee got the socks","Dee","I got the socks","Marty","I got the sorghum, and a little boy at the church gave me a drawing of the feed store with a big antenna on top, and a cat sitting on the antenna that's bigger than the store","Marty","That's accurate, that's exactly how it is around here - count your people - Merry Christmas - good night"}},
{"r5_obit_hollis_painted_pinecones","obituary",170,170,8,12,8,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning, it's the day after Christmas, and a Sunday, and I'll confess I didn't know what to say this week until yesterday afternoon","Reverend Hollis","Yesterday a boy of about ten knocked on the parsonage door with a coffee can full of pinecones he'd painted with house paint - Ornaments, he's giving them to anybody who's lost someone","Reverend Hollis","He wouldn't give his name, he said his mother told him never to give his name to anybody - good for her","Reverend Hollis","So I'll read his pinecones instead, everyone who asked for one had a name painted on the bottom","Reverend Hollis","Roy and Delores Tipton, baby Grace Hardin - coach Bill Estes - mamaw Sue, and Everett, no last name, just Everett","Reverend Hollis","If one of those pinecones is on your windowsill this morning, there's a boy's kindness in your house - that's the sermon, I couldn't improve on it"}},
{"r9_trade_d172_hen_for_a_hen","trade",172,250,9,16,1,{"Caller - Vesta","Marty, this sounds foolish out loud, but I want to trade a hen for a hen","Marty","Explain it for the town people, Vesta","Caller - Vesta","My rooster is granddaddy, daddy and uncle to every bird in my lot - keep that up two more years and you get chicks that don't hatch and hens that don't make it to the fall","Caller - Vesta","So I want somebody else's bird, any bird from a lot that's got nothing to do with mine - pullet for a pullet, straight across, and neither one of us is out a thing","Marty","How far does a bird need to come?","Caller - Vesta","Another road's plenty, another town's better - and spare me a young rooster, I'll trade two hens and think I won","Dee","Carry them in a box with air holes and keep them away from your own birds a week when you get home - new bird, new sickness, every single time","Marty","That's a good one, folks, that's people planning for a year out, the Wickham road, the house with the blue barn, any afternoon"}},
{"r5_host_new_year_resolutions","host",174,176,0,23,5,{"Dee","New Year's resolutions - Marty, you go first","Marty","I resolve to sleep four hours straight without somebody hollering 'Marty' in my ear","Dee","That was one time, and you were on fire","Marty","My sleeve was smoking, smoking is not on fire","Dee","It was on fire, everybody, I put it out with a bag of rabbit pellets","Dee","Mine is to write 'doing better' at the bottom of more charts this year","Marty","That's a good one, happy nineteen ninety-four, Knox County - I wasn't sure we'd get to say that"}},
{"r3_so_d176_nineteen_ninety_four","sign_on",176,176,6,9,10,{"Marty","Good morning, it's nineteen ninety-four - Dee says I have to say it out loud or it doesn't count","Dee","It counts, it's nineteen ninety-four","Marty","Last night at midnight, fourteen people at the church stood out in the cold and said happy new year in a whisper, all together - I never heard anything that quiet sound so much like a party","Marty","Resolutions, mine is to fix the drip over the back office - I made that same one last year, before all this - the drip's still here, so am I - it's {time}"}},
{"r9_joke_d176_walking_strategy","caller_joke",176,255,16,22,1,{"Caller - Willard","Marty, I'm fifty-one and I've got a knee that's been wrong since seventy-nine, so I can't run - not a step","Marty","So what do you do?","Caller - Willard","I've got a system, I walk everywhere like I'm already late - not fast - steady, I never stand still in an open place and I never go anywhere I haven't already picked out the door","Marty","That's better thinking than most people's","Caller - Willard","It's not thinking, Marty, it's that I can't run, all my good habits are things I couldn't get out of","Caller - Willard","Young fellows just run, everywhere, straight lines, right on past the door","Marty","You want to give them one piece of advice?","Caller - Willard","Hurt your knee"}},
{"r9_ins_d178_pump_wont_freeze","instruction",178,255,8,20,1,{"Marty","The water part of winter - Ruel, you're on - go ahead and tell them about the pump","Caller - Ruel","A hand pump freezes because you left water standing in the barrel of it - that's all, pump it dry every time - last stroke, let it come up empty, and then walk off","Caller - Ruel","If it's already froze, do not pour boiling water on that cast iron - you'll crack the barrel and then it's a fence post - warm water, rags, and time","Marty","And a pipe in the house?","Caller - Ruel","A dripping faucet don't freeze, if you've still got pressure off a tank, leave one dripping at the far end of the run and open the cabinet doors under the sink so what heat's in the room can get at the pipe","Dee","And keep water inside overnight, two buckets in the room you're heating, covered, if you have to go out at four in the morning and thaw a pump before anybody drinks, that's a bad morning waiting on you","Marty","Snow is not water, you can melt it, but it takes about ten times what you'd think and you'll burn wood doing it - melt it, then boil it, and don't eat it cold out of the yard"}},
{"r3_host_d180_mail_slot_froze","host",180,230,0,23,1,{"Marty","The mail slot froze shut last week, somebody went to the trouble of prying it open with a screwdriver just to push a note through","Marty","The note says, 'Mail slot is froze.' That's all it says","Marty","I've been thinking about that man walking however far in the snow to tell me my mail slot's froze, and I believe he's the most Kentucky thing that's happened all winter","Marty","Thank you, sir, I thawed it, I poured a kettle of hot water on it, it's froze again"}},
{"r5_trade_roundup_winter","trade",180,230,9,16,1,{"Dee","Winter Trading Post, and this is everything you called in about while Marty was napping","Marty","I was resting my eyes","Dee","A man in Riverside has tire chains that fit a pickup, and he wants a bag of flour - Riverside boat ramp lot, eleven AM","Dee","Two wool Army blankets in Muldraugh for a box of shotgun shells - no, sir - call back with something else","Marty","A family in March Ridge needs a six-inch stovepipe elbow - they'll trade a rocking chair, they say it rocks - that's all they told us","Dee","Somebody in West Point has a whole pallet of rock salt for the ice - Marty wants you to know he is not jealous","Marty","I'm not, I've got salt - I have a great deal of salt","Dee","West Point town hall parking lot, noon, for canned meat - and whoever's trading, go early, it's dark by five-thirty now"}},
{"r5_host_dee_flu_arms_checked","host",180,240,0,23,1,{"Marty","Dee's on the cot with a fever of a hundred and one - she's been telling me how to take care of her for three hours straight","Dee","Fluids - every hour, you forgot at four","Marty","She's ordered me to tell you she's fine","Dee","I'm fine","Marty","She is not fine - she's bossy, it's the flu, and she's certain it's the flu - no scratches, no bites, I checked her arms myself","Marty","And she let me, which is how I know she's sick","Dee","Fluids, Marty"}},
{"r9_obit_d184_hollis_bulletin_typist","obituary",184,184,8,12,8,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning, it's the ninth of January and this is the coldest I have ever been in a building with a roof on it","Reverend Hollis","Ova Tackett, of March Ridge, who typed the church bulletin every Saturday for twenty-six years and never one time misspelled anybody's name, and there are some hard ones in this congregation","Reverend Hollis","The last one she typed is for the eleventh of July and it's still in the box in the vestibule - there's a hymn number on it and a line about the ice cream social","Reverend Hollis","Isom Kite, of Ekron, eighty-eight, a mule man, who was the last person in this county who could tell you the names of the two mules that pulled the grader on the Echo Creek road when he was a boy","Reverend Hollis","Maudie Renfro, of Rosewood, who took in four children in the fifties that were not hers and never called them anything but hers","Reverend Hollis","I'm hoarse and I'm cold this morning and I've got no sermon, just the names, that's all I brought"}},
{"r9_sil_d185_wendell_water_bowl_ice","silence",185,260,6,10,1,{"Marty","Stand by a minute - Wendell's bowl's froze solid again and he's stood there looking at me about it","Marty","That's the fourth morning, he don't paw at it or bark - he just looks at me, then at the bowl, then at me","Marty","I've started keeping a jug inside for it, takes about a minute - it's the only thing all day I know how to fix"}},
{"r3_wx_d186_deer_on_the_creek","weather",186,200,6,10,1,{"Marty","Weather - cold, cold enough that the creek behind the store froze clear across, and I watched a deer walk over it this morning like it was a road","Marty","Single digits today, below zero again tonight, wind out of the north makes it feel a good deal worse","Marty","The ice on that creek will not hold you, it held the deer - the deer weighs a lot less than you, and the deer doesn't care if it goes through","Marty","Stay in, bring the dogs in - bring the chickens in if you have to - I did - Dee is not speaking to me"}},
{"r9_so_d186_almost_didnt_come_in","sign_on",186,235,6,9,1,{"Marty","Morning, this is ninety-nine point six, it's {time} and I'm already tired","Marty","I'm going to be honest with you about this morning - I sat in the truck in my own parking lot about twenty minutes and thought hard about going back home and getting in the bed","Marty","I'm not telling you that so anybody worries, I'm telling you because I'd bet money nine out of ten of you did the same thing at your own door and thought you were the only one","Dee","He came in - he's here, his coffee's about the color of creek water and he's drinking it","Marty","I came in, let's do the list"}},
{"r3_so_d190_twenty_two_below","sign_on",190,196,6,9,3,{"Marty","Morning, it's twenty-two below zero on the grain bin thermometer - I tapped it, it stayed put","Marty","I've lived in this county fifty-six years and never once seen that - if you're hearing this, you made it through the night, and that's all you've got to do today","Marty","Don't go out, whatever it is, don't - keep the fire going, keep everybody in the one room, and don't touch metal with a bare hand","Marty","I haven't seen one of them moving on the road since yesterday noon - I don't know if that's the cold, or if they're just somewhere else - don't go find out - it's {time}"}},
{"r3_ins_d190_one_warm_room_too_long","instruction",190,240,0,23,1,{"Dee","It's February, everybody's been shut up in one warm room since December, and I can hear it on nineteen - people snapping at each other, people not getting out of bed","Dee","You're not being weak, it's winter and a year like this one, piled on top of each other","Dee","So, everybody gets out of the room once a day, in daylight, even if it's only to the woodpile and back - everybody gets a job, even the ones who are too sad to do it - especially them","Dee","And if somebody in your house quits eating, or starts giving their things away, or talks about being a burden, don't leave them by themselves - tell me, it ain't gossip - call it medicine"}},
{"r5_host_horse_blanket_snow","host",190,215,0,23,1,{"Marty","We are broadcasting tonight in coats, gloves, and in my case, a horse blanket","Dee","It's a clean horse blanket","Marty","It's a clean-ish horse blanket, I sold it new in nineteen eighty-nine, and it came back to me in a trade last week, so it's had a life","Dee","The snow's about ten inches on the loading dock, the tracks out front are mostly deer - not all of them","Marty","If you have to go out in this, turn around and look at your tracks - you're drawing a line straight back to your own door","Dee","Stay in if you can, burn what you've got - we'll be here when it thaws"}},
{"r5_joke_bev_bird_feeder","caller_joke",190,225,17,22,1,{"Caller - Bev","Marty, it's so cold out here that the one in my side yard froze stiff standing up - hasn't moved in four days","Marty","Bev, keep your distance - they thaw","Caller - Bev","Oh, I know it, I'm just making use of him for now","Marty","Making use of him how?","Caller - Bev","I hung the bird feeder off his arm, the cardinals love it, he doesn't mind, the birds don't mind","Caller - Bev","Leonard minds - Leonard won't look out the kitchen window anymore"}},
{"r9_trade_d190_trash_and_a_check_in","trade",190,260,9,16,1,{"Marty","This next note is a trade the way a fish is a bicycle, but she wrote it as a trade so I'll read it as a trade","Marty","Miz Almeda Sipes, out behind the Ekron post office, she says she'll give a jar of chow-chow to whoever will come haul off what she can't carry to the burn pile","Dee","She's eighty-three and she has got nine cats and about a hundred feet of driveway","Marty","So I'm going to be plain about what this note is - she doesn't need the chow-chow gone, she needs somebody to come up that driveway twice a month and say her name to her","Dee","And she'll act put out about it when you come - let her, she'll have coffee made","Marty","If you're out that way, that's the trade, haul her trash, take the jar, and sit down in that kitchen fifteen minutes whether you've got fifteen minutes or not","Marty","And there's about nine more of these in my ledger - if that one sounded like something you could do, key up and I'll give you another one"}},
{"r5_obit_hollis_frozen_ground","obituary",191,191,8,12,8,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning, it's a cold one - the thermometer on the parsonage porch says four degrees, and I believe it's being generous","Reverend Hollis","The ground's frozen hard, and three families have asked me this week how to bury someone - I'll tell you what we did at the church, we wrapped them, kept them in the cold shed, and waited for a thaw - there's no shame in waiting","Reverend Hollis","This week's names","Reverend Hollis","Bernice Carrico, of Ekron, who crocheted a blanket for every baby baptized at her church since nineteen fifty-one - somebody counted once, two hundred and eight","Reverend Hollis","Leon Terry, of Muldraugh, who plowed the church lot every snow without being asked, and drove off before anybody could hand him a cup of coffee","Reverend Hollis","And Ada Fields, of West Point, who wrote me every week this winter to ask how I was - nobody had asked me that in a long time, her last letter was mostly about the weather","Reverend Hollis","Keep your stoves banked and your neighbors close - God keep you this week"}},
{"r9_sf_d192_dee_sick_marty_alone","sign_off",192,240,21,23,1,{"Marty","Signing off, and it's just me tonight - Dee is in the back with a fever and she has been told she is not allowed in this chair until Thursday","Marty","So if you called with something medical today and got a man reading out of a first aid book, that was me, and I want to apologize for how that went","Marty","I told a woman something about a burn that I got out of the book, and Dee heard it through the wall and hollered the right answer, and the right answer was different - cool water - twenty minutes, no butter, no grease, no ice","Marty","Twenty minutes is longer than you think it is - stand there and count it, that's from her, not from me, and hers is the one you want","Marty","Good night, and spare a thought for the woman in my back room"}},
{"r3_host_d196_under_the_desk","host",196,210,0,23,6,{"Marty","Something happened last night I want to tell you about, because Dee can't get through it yet, and she's asked me to","Marty","Around one in the morning a man came up on nineteen asking if the feed store in March Ridge still had a truck it could lend out - said he needed to move a couch","Marty","I heard the chair go over, I came out of the back and Dee was sitting on the floor under the desk with the mic in her lap - just sitting there","Marty","It's Curtis, he's with that Guard bunch north of here - he's been fixing their trucks since August, and he didn't know there was a station till a man came through trading fuel","Dee","He laughed, on the radio - that's how I knew, before he ever said his name - nobody else in the world laughs like that","Marty","He's coming down Thursday - Dee says he is not getting the truck"}},
{"r9_ins_d196_split_hands","instruction",196,270,8,20,1,{"Dee","Hands, and I've earned the right to say this one - half of you have got splits in your fingers right now and you're treating it like weather","Dee","A crack at the knuckle or the fingertip is an open wound - I'm not being dramatic, it's open every time you make a fist","Dee","At night, wash, dry all the way, then grease them and put a sock on your hand - lard, bag balm, petroleum jelly, bacon grease if that's what you've got - a sock over it so it stays on you and not on the quilt","Dee","In the day, a strip of tape over the split before you go pick up a piece of wire or a jar or a feed sack - tape's cheaper than what I've got left in the bag","Marty","Tell them the red line","Dee","A red line running up from a cut toward your elbow, don't wait on that one, come find me, I'll get out of bed for it","Marty","Mine went about a week of that before I did what she said - don't be me, I'm not a good example of anything but stubbornness"}},
{"r9_host_d198_curtis_walked_in","host",198,215,0,23,10,{"Marty","I've got to do this careful because I've been wrong before and I will not do that to anybody again","Marty","At about four o'clock this afternoon a man walked up the drive in Army coveralls and stood in my lot and would not come to the door","Marty","So I went out, and he asked me, is the nurse here, and I said which nurse, and he said, my sister","Marty","Folks, I've read the name Curtis Meade on this radio one hundred and some nights - he is sat on a pallet of sweet feed eating out of a can with his hands shaking","Dee","I'm not going to talk right now, Marty","Marty","She's not going to talk right now, she sat down on the floor when she saw him and she's still on the floor","Marty","Eight names left on tonight's list - eight, I'll read them at eleven and I'll read them tomorrow"}},
{"r9_obit_d198_hollis_no_name_boots","obituary",198,198,8,12,8,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning - Marty tells me my voice sounds like a gravel road, and Dee says I'm to be off this radio in ten minutes, and she's stood right there with her watch, so","Reverend Hollis","Two names and a third thing","Reverend Hollis","Zelma Yount, of the Muldraugh road, who got a card from her boy at basic in ninety-two asking for socks, and who kept the card in her Bible at the Twenty-third Psalm, which is where her daughter found it","Reverend Hollis","Estel Combs, of West Point, who fixed two things in this building without being asked and would not take a dime for either one, and who fixed the pump at the parsonage while I was asleep and never told me","Reverend Hollis","And the third thing, we buried a man on the Ekron road Thursday and we do not know his name - grown, fifty or so, a wedding band and a work jacket with the name tore off it","Reverend Hollis","We buried him with his boots on because we couldn't get them off him and I would not have a man cut on for a pair of boots - he's under the third elm at Little Bethel with a stone I wrote on in pencil","Reverend Hollis","If you're missing a man, come look at the jacket - I've kept it, I've kept all of them, there's four jackets in a box in my office now"}},
{"r3_sf_d200_busted_muffler","sign_off",200,260,0,2,1,{"Dee","Signing off, my brother's asleep on the cot, and he snores like a busted muffler, and I've been sitting here listening to it on purpose","Dee","I want to say something to everybody still waiting on somebody - I know how it sounds, coming from me right now - I'm not telling you it'll happen, I'm telling you I'm not going to quit saying names on this radio","Dee","Good night, ninety-nine point six"}},
{"r3_ins_d200_seed_in_coffee_cans","instruction",200,260,6,12,1,{"Marty","Seed, this is the most important thing I'll say all winter, and it's going to sound boring","Marty","The seed rack at the store is about empty, there's no seed shipment coming, not this year, not any year, what we plant this spring has to come from what we save","Marty","Beans, tomatoes, squash, peppers, you can save - let a few go past eating, dry the seed on a plate, and keep it in a jar somewhere cool and dark where the mice can't get it - label it","Marty","The seed corn you find in bags is hybrid, it won't come back true from its own seed, plant it this year - save from the old open-pollinated corn if anybody has it - ask the old folks, it's in coffee cans in their pantries","Marty","Seed potatoes, cut them so every piece has two eyes, let them dry a day, then plant - don't eat your seed potatoes this winter - I know - don't"}},
{"r3_sil_d200_week_without_diesel","silence",200,300,7,10,1,{"Marty","We were off the air a week, out of diesel - I won't dress it up","Marty","Curtis drove down from the Guard post with four cans in the back of an Army truck he says he's borrowing - we're back, thank you to everybody who kept nineteen going without us","Dee","Harold ran the noon check-in, all of it, in one breath"}},
{"r5_host_marty_voice_gone","host",200,260,0,23,1,{"Dee","Marty's lost his voice, so he's writing on the backs of feed invoices and holding them up, and I'm reading them to you","Dee","The first one says, 'Tell them I'm fine.' He's not fine - he sounds like a gravel truck backing up","Dee","Now he's written, 'The nurse is exaggerating.' That's underlined twice","Dee","This one's longer - 'tell them I'd rather lose my voice than lose the station.' He's pointing at it - he wants me to read it again, I'm not going to","Dee","Now he's written 'honey and whiskey.' We have neither, he knows we have neither - he wrote it anyway","Dee","Salt water, Marty - Gargle, and put that pencil down, you're using up the invoices"}},
{"r5_joke_bernard_toupee","caller_joke",200,400,17,22,1,{"Caller - Bernard","Marty, I've quit wearing my toupee","Marty","Well, Bernard, there's not much call for it these days","Caller - Bernard","That's what I figured, nobody left to fool","Caller - Bernard","Then I caught myself in a truck mirror and about jumped out of my shoes - thought one of them had snuck up on me","Caller - Bernard","Turns out the only person that toupee was ever fooling was me"}},
{"r5_obit_marty_dee_turns_list","obituary",200,400,8,21,1,{"Marty","We've got a long list today, so Dee and I are going to take turns - one name, one thing about them, that's how people wrote them in","Marty","Carl Yates, of Ekron, he gave a ride to anybody standing on 31W for thirty years and never once got robbed - he said it was because he talked too much","Dee","Rosa Delgado, of West Point, she ran the laundromat and sewed your buttons back on for free if you left the shirt on the folding table","Marty","Hobart Clemmons, of March Ridge, he sat on the bench outside my store from seven to eight every morning and told me the weather - he was wrong every day for nine years","Dee","Tanya Rudd, nineteen, of Muldraugh, she ran a register at the grocery and taught herself sign language so she could talk to one customer","Marty","Frank and Lois Keel, of Riverside, they drove to Florida every February for forty winters and mailed a postcard to their whole church every time","Dee","Denny Whitlock, of Brandenburg, little League coach, he made the worst player on the team keep the scorebook, so nobody ever just sat on the bench","Marty","Myrtle Shain, of Rosewood, ninety-eight, the note says she was ready, she was mean as a snake, and everybody loved her","Dee","That's today's list - if your person's not on it, they're in the stack, we'll get to them"}},
}
